1. Neo4j Cypher 25 grammar (generated parser)

   Files:   src/cypher-interp/generated/Cypher25Lexer.ts
            src/cypher-interp/generated/Cypher25Parser.ts
   Source:  Cypher25Lexer.g4 and Cypher25Parser.g4 from the npm package
            @neo4j-cypher/language-support 2.0.0-next.38
            (https://github.com/neo4j/cypher-language-support)
   Owner:   Copyright (c) "Neo4j", Neo4j Sweden AB [https://neo4j.com]
   Licence: Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt,
            also http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)

   The two files are generated from the grammar by antlr-ng 1.0.10 with
   scripts/v1.3/gen-cypher-parser.sh. Modifications: the grammar's one Java
   lexer action (RCURLY: `if (!_modeStack.isEmpty()) popMode();`) is replaced
   by its TypeScript form (`if (this.modeStack.length > 0) this.popMode();`),
   as upstream's own CypherCmdLexer.g4 does; lint/type-check suppression
   comments are added. Each file carries the grammar's original copyright and
   licence header verbatim.

   The grammar is pinned to a prerelease because the package has never
   published a non-prerelease version: its `latest` dist-tag (2.0.0-next.6,
   2024) ships only the older Cypher 5 grammar and does not export the grammar
   files. See scripts/v1.3/gen-cypher-parser.sh and
   Docs/v1.3/cypher-interpreter.md section 2.1.

   The upstream package ships no NOTICE file of its own.

